H7000.definition:
a primitive root;
to inclose
KJV: join.

H7001.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H7000 (קָטַר);
a knot (as tied up), i.e. (figuratively) a riddle; also a vertebra (as if a knot)
KJV: doubt, joint.

H7003.definition:
from H6999 (קָטַר); fumigative;
Kitron, a place in Palestine
KJV: Kitron.

H7004.definition:
from H6999 (קָטַר);
a fumigation
KJV: (sweet) incense, perfume.

H7005.definition:
from H6996 (קָטָן); littleness;
Kattath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Kattath.

H7006.definition:
a primitive root;
to vomit
KJV: spue.

H7007.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7019 (קַיִץ);
harvest
KJV: summer.

H7008.definition:
or קִיטֹר; from H6999 (קָטַר);
a fume, i.e. cloud
KJV: smoke, vapour.

H7009.definition:
from H6965 (קוּם);
an opponent (as rising against one), i.e. (collectively) enemies
KJV: substance.

H7010.definition:
(Aramaic) from H6966 (קוּם);
an edict (as arising in law)
KJV: decree, statute.

H7011.definition:
(Aramaic) from H6966 (קוּם);
permanent (as rising firmly)
KJV: stedfast, sure.

H7012.definition:
from H6965 (קוּם);
an arising
KJV: rising up.

H7013.definition:
from H6969 (קוּן) in the original sense of fixity;
a lance (as striking fast)
KJV: spear.

H7014.definition:
the same as H7013 (קַיִן) (with a play upon the affinity to H7069 (קָנָה));
Kajin, the name of the first child, also of a place in Palestine, and of an Oriental tribe
KJV: Cain, Kenite(-s).

H7015.definition:
from H6969 (קוּן);
a dirge (as accompanied by beating the breasts or on instruments)
KJV: lamentation.

H7016.definition:
the same as H7015 (קִינָה);
Kinah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Kinah.

H7017.definition:
or קִינִי; (1 Chronicles 2:55), patronymic from H7014 (קַיִן);
a Kenite or member of the tribe of Kajin
KJV: Kenite.

H7018.definition:
from the same as H7064 (קֵן); fixed;
Kenan, an antediluvian
KJV: Cainan, Kenan.

H7019.definition:
from H6972 (קוּץ);
harvest (as the crop), whether the product (grain or fruit) or the (dry) season
KJV: summer (fruit, house).

H7020.definition:
from H6972 (קוּץ);
terminal
KJV: out-(utter-) most.

H7021.definition:
perhaps from H7006 (קָיָה);
the gourd (as nauseous)
KJV: gourd.

H7022.definition:
from H7036 (קָלוֹן);
intense disgrace
KJV: shameful spewing.

H7023.definition:
or קִר; (Isaiah 22:5), or (feminine) קִירָה; from H6979 (קוּר);
a wall (as built in a trench)
KJV: [phrase] mason, side, town, [idiom] very, wall.

H7024.definition:
the same as H7023 (קִיר); fortress;
Kir, a place in Assyrian; also one in Moab
KJV: Kir. Compare H7025 (קִיר חֶרֶשׂ).

H7025.definition:
or (feminine of the latter word) קִיר חֲרֶשֶׂת; from H7023 (קִיר) and H2789 (חֶרֶשׂ); fortress of earthenware;
Kir-Cheres or Kir-Chareseth, a place in Moab
KJV: Kir-haraseth, Kir-hareseth, Kirharesh, Kir-heres.

H7026.definition:
or קֵרֹס; from the same as H7166 (קַרְסֹל); ankled;
Keros, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Keros.

H7027.definition:
from H6983 (קוֹשׁ); a bow;
Kish, the name of five Israelites
KJV: Kish.

H7028.definition:
from H6983 (קוֹשׁ); winding;
Kishon, a river of Palestine
KJV: Kishon, Kison.

H7029.definition:
from H6983 (קוֹשׁ); bowed;
Kishi, an Israelite
KJV: Kishi.

H7030.definition:
(Aramaic) of Greek origin;
a lyre
KJV: harp.

H7031.definition:
contracted from H7043 (קָלַל);
light; (by implication) rapid (also adverbial)
KJV: light, swift(-ly).

H7032.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6963 (קוֹל)
{a voice or sound}
KJV: sound, voice.

H7033.definition:
a primitive root (rather identical with H7034 (קָלָה) through the idea of shrinkage by heat);
to toast, i.e. scorch partially or slowly
KJV: dried, loathsome, parch, roast.

H7034.definition:
a primitive root;
to be light (as implied in rapid motion), but figuratively, only (be (causatively, hold) in contempt)
KJV: base, contemn, despise, lightly esteem, set light, seem vile.

H7035.definition:
for H6950 (קָהַל);
to assemble
KJV: gather together.

H7036.definition:
from H7034 (קָלָה);
disgrace; (by implication) the pudenda
KJV: confusion, dishonour, ignominy, reproach, shame.

H7037.definition:
apparently but a form for H6747 (צַלַּחַת);
a kettle
KJV: caldron.

H7038.definition:
a primitive root;
to maim
KJV: lacking in his parts.

H7039.definition:
or קָלִיא; from H7033 (קָלָה);
roasted ears of grain
KJV: parched corn.

H7040.definition:
from H7043 (קָלַל); frivolous;
Kallai, an Israelite
KJV: Kallai.

H7041.definition:
from H7034 (קָלָה); insignificance;
Kelajah, an Israelite
KJV: Kelaiah.

H7042.definition:
from H7038 (קָלַט); maiming;
Kelita, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Kelita.

H7043.definition:
a primitive root;
to be (causatively, make) light, literally (swift, small, sharp, etc.) or figuratively (easy, trifling, vile, etc.)
KJV: abate, make bright, bring into contempt, (ac-) curse, despise, (be) ease(-y, -ier), (be a, make, make somewhat, move, seem a, set) light(-en, -er, -ly, -ly afflict, -ly esteem, thing), [idiom] slight(-ly), be swift(-er), (be, be more, make, re-) vile, whet.

H7044.definition:
from H7043 (קָלַל);
brightened (as if sharpened)
KJV: burnished, polished.

H7046.definition:
a primitive root;
to disparage, i.e. ridicule
KJV: mock, scoff, scorn.

H7047.definition:
from H7046 (קָלַס);
a laughing-stock
KJV: derision.

H7048.definition:
intensive from H7046 (קָלַס);
ridicule
KJV: mocking.

H7049.definition:
a primitive root;
to sling; also to carve (as if a circular motion, or into light forms)
KJV: carve, sling (out).

H7050.definition:
from H7049 (קָלַע);
a sling; also a (door) screen (as if slung across), or the valve (of the door) itself
KJV: hanging, leaf, sling.

H7051.definition:
intensive from H7049 (קָלַע);
a slinger
KJV: slinger.

H7053.definition:
from an unused root meaning to prick;
a prong, i.e. hay-fork
KJV: fork.

H7054.definition:
feminine of active participle of H6965 (קוּם);
something that rises, i.e. a stalk of grain
KJV: (standing) corn, grown up, stalk.

H7055.definition:
from H6965 (קוּם) and H410 (אֵל); raised of God;
Kemuel, the name of a relative of Abraham, and of two Israelites
KJV: Kemuel.

H7056.definition:
from H6965 (קוּם); an elevation;
Kamon, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Camon.

H7057.definition:
or קִימוֹשׁ; from an unused root meaning to sting;
a prickly plant
KJV: nettle. Compare H7063 (קִמָּשׁוֹן).

H7058.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to grind;
flour
KJV: flour, meal.

H7059.definition:
a primitive root;
to pluck, i.e. destroy
KJV: cut down, fill with wrinkles.

H7060.definition:
a primitive root;
to wither
KJV: hew down, wither.

H7061.definition:
a primitive root;
to grasp with the hand
KJV: take an handful.

H7062.definition:
from H7061 (קָמַץ);
a grasp, i.e. handful
KJV: handful.

H7063.definition:
from the same as H7057 (קִמּוֹשׁ);
a prickly plant
KJV: thorn.

H7064.definition:
contracted from H7077 (קָנַן);
a nest (as fixed), sometimes including the nestlings; figuratively, a chamber or dwelling
KJV: nest, room.

H7065.definition:
a primitive root;
to be (causatively, make) zealous, i.e. (in a bad sense) jealous or envious
KJV: (be) envy(-ious), be (move to, provoke to) jealous(-y), [idiom] very, (be) zeal(-ous).

H7066.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7069 (קָנָה);
to purchase
KJV: buy.

H7067.definition:
from H7065 (קָנָא);
jealous
KJV: jealous. Compare H7072 (קַנּוֹא).

H7068.definition:
from H7065 (קָנָא);
jealousy or envy
KJV: envy(-ied), jealousy, [idiom] sake, zeal.

H7069.definition:
a primitive root;
to erect, i.e. create; by extension, to procure, especially by purchase (causatively, sell); by implication to own
KJV: attain, buy(-er), teach to keep cattle, get, provoke to jealousy, possess(-or), purchase, recover, redeem, [idiom] surely, [idiom] verily.

H7070.definition:
from H7069 (קָנָה);
a reed (as erect); by resemblance a rod (especially for measuring), shaft, tube, stem, the radius (of the arm), beam (of a steelyard)
KJV: balance, bone, branch, calamus, cane, reed, [idiom] spearman, stalk.

H7071.definition:
feminine of H7070 (קָנֶה); reediness;
Kanah, the name of a stream and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Kanah.

H7072.definition:
for H7067 (קַנָּא);
jealous or angry
KJV: jealous.

H7073.definition:
probably from an unused root meaning to hunt; hunter;
Kenaz, the name of an Edomite and of two Israelites
KJV: Kenaz.

H7075.definition:
from H7069 (קָנָה);
creation, i.e. (concretely) creatures; also acquisition, purchase, wealth
KJV: getting, goods, [idiom] with money, riches, substance.

H7076.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to erect);
cinnamon bark (as in upright rolls)
KJV: cinnamon.

H7077.definition:
a primitive root; to erect; but used only as denominative from H7064 (קֵן);
to nestle, i.e. build or occupy as anest
KJV: make...nest.

H7078.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to wrench;
perversion
KJV: end.

H7079.definition:
from H7069 (קָנָה); possession;
Kenath, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Kenath.

H7080.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to distribute, i.e. determine by lot or magical scroll; by implication, to divine
KJV: divine(-r, -ation), prudent, soothsayer, use (divination).

H7081.definition:
from H7080 (קָסַם);
a lot; also divination (including its fee), oracle
KJV: (reward of) divination, divine sentence, witchcraft.

H7082.definition:
a primitive root;
to lop off
KJV: cut off.

H7083.definition:
from the same as H3563 (כּוֹס) (or as H7185 (קָשָׁה));
properly, a cup, i.e. an ink-stand
KJV: inkhorn.

H7084.definition:
perhaps from H7049 (קָלַע) in the sense of enclosing; citadel;
Keilah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Keilah.

H7085.definition:
from the same as H6970 (קוֹעַ);
an incision or gash
KJV: [phrase] mark.

H7086.definition:
probably from H7167 (קָרַע);
a bowl (as cut out hollow)
KJV: charger, dish.

H7087.definition:
a primitive root;
to shrink, i.e. thicken (as unracked wine, curdled milk, clouded sky, frozen water)
KJV: congeal, curdle, dark, settle.

H7088.definition:
a primitive root;
to contract, i.e. roll together
KJV: cut off.

H7089.definition:
from H7088 (קָפַד);
shrinking, i.e., terror
KJV: destruction.

H7090.definition:
or קִפֹּדlemma קִכֹּד kaf, corrected to קִפֹּד; from H7088 (קָפַד);
a species of bird, perhaps the bittern (from its contracted form)
KJV: bittern.

H7092.definition:
a primitive root;
to draw together, i.e. close; by implication, to leap (by contracting the limbs); specifically, to die (from gathering up the feet)
KJV: shut (up), skip, stop, take out of the way.

H7093.definition:
contracted from H7112 (קָצַץ);
an extremity; adverbially (with prepositional prefix) after
KJV: [phrase] after, (utmost) border, end, (in-) finite, [idiom] process.

H7094.definition:
a primitive root;
to clip, or (generally) chop
KJV: cut down, shorn.

H7095.definition:
from H7094 (קָצַב);
shape (as if cut out); base (as if there cut off)
KJV: bottom, size.

H7096.definition:
a primitive root;
to cut off; (figuratively) to destroy; (partially) to scrape off
KJV: cut off, cut short, scrape (off).
